{"name":"Scarlet Tanager","hex":"#b43b3d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scarlet tanager","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Piranga olivacea, a medium-sized American songbird. Adult males are crimson-red with black wings and tail."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarlet_tanager"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scarlet tanager","blocks":[{"text":"The scarlet tanager is a medium-sized American songbird in the cardinal family (Cardinalidae). It was placed in the tanager family (Thraupidae) until 2009, but was moved to Cardinalidae following several genetic studies indicating the Piranga tanagers are more closely related to cardinals and their allies. Breeding males have bright red plumage with black wings and tails, while females are yellow-olive. Outside the breeding season, males develop plumage similar to that of females, although their wings and tails remain darker. \nThe species breeds mainly in large deciduous forests in eastern North America. It migrates through Central America to spend the winter in forests along the Andean foothills of northwestern South America. Scarlet tanagers feed mainly on insects, but they also eat fruit when it is available. Habitat fragmentation can increase nest predation and brood parasitism, and populations are declining in some areas. However, the species is classified as Least Concern by the International Union for Conservation of Nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Scarlet_tanager_in_GWC_%2850867%29.jpg/330px-Scarlet_tanager_in_GWC_%2850867%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_tanager","wikidata":"Q1193366"},{"title":"Tanager","blocks":[{"text":"The tanagers comprise the bird family Thraupidae, in the order Passeriformes. The family has a Neotropical distribution and is the second-largest family of birds. It represents about 4% of all avian species and 12% of the Neotropical birds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Thraupidae_Diversity.jpg/330px-Thraupidae_Diversity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanager","wikidata":"Q666222"},{"title":"Scarlet (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Scarlet is a bright red color, sometimes with a slightly orange tinge. In the spectrum of visible light, and on the traditional color wheel, it is one-quarter of the way between red and orange, slightly less orange than vermilion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/RCMP-female-officer.jpg/330px-RCMP-female-officer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarlet_(color)","wikidata":"Q2268159"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg/500px-Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg/1280px-Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg/500px-Piranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_%2815359865237%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiranga_olivacea_Piranga_alinegra_Scarlet_Tanager_(15359865237).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/ScarletTanager_mosbo6.jpg/500px-ScarletTanager_mosbo6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con